/* ===== RELIGIOUS STUDIES · PASHTO (faith pack, July 2026) =====
   PRIMARILY FOR PASHTO SPEAKERS (Afghanistan) to learn about Jesus —
   Pashto is the primary language everywhere (titles, story text,
   explanations), with English the quiet second line. Mirrors faith/ne.js:
   the same two stories, the same 10+10 big-moment sections, the same
   shared scene art. Deliberately Christian (the secular-content rule does
   NOT apply in faith mode). Content register: rich storytelling for the
   un-churched reader — every person, place and church-word introduced
   in-story on first use (Adam & Eve, Eden, Noah, Abraham, sacrifice, the
   prophets, exile, disciples, Mary Magdalene). Paraphrase only — no
   Bible-translation text is copied; references name the passages retold.
   PASHTO IS RIGHT-TO-LEFT. The faith reader gets its own RTL rule in
   index.html next to the course RTL pass (the .fpara / .fne / .fnote
   blocks flow rtl for :root[data-lang="ps"]); Arabic-script runs already
   shape correctly on their own, this is about block alignment.
   Vocabulary — taken from the AFGHAN Pashto Bible (afghanbibles.org),
   verified against its Luke 19 and Luke 24 text, so the wording matches
   what Pashto Christian materials actually use rather than a guess:
   خدای (God), څښتن (Lord), عیسی / عیسی مسیح (Jesus), زوی (Son),
   ګناه (sin), ګناهکار (sinner), خلاصون (salvation), پاچاهي (kingdom),
   صلیب (cross), راژوندی کېدل (to rise from the dead), شاګردان
   (disciples), پیغمبران (prophets), زېری / ښه زېری (good news, gospel),
   باور / ایمان (believe / faith), مینه (love), روح القدس (Holy Spirit),
   تړون (covenant), قربانی (sacrifice), وعده (promise), پرښته (angel),
   وری (lamb), بپتسما (baptism), دعا (prayer), د انسان زوی (Son of Man).
   Note خدای and عیسی are the ordinary Pashto words a Muslim reader
   already knows — that is deliberate and matches the Afghan Pashto Bible;
   the story itself does the teaching.
   Romanization follows the Pashto course scheme in lang/ps.js (ASCII;
   schwa written a; long alif aa; retroflexes doubled tt dd rr nn;
   څ=ts, ځ=dz, ښ=x, ږ=g, خ=kh, غ=gh; ع not written). Native strings must
   avoid the chars ' " < > \ (they ride inline onclick handlers).
   IMPORTANT: keep paras[i][0] AND note[0] byte-stable once audio exists —
   clips in audio-psf/ are hashed from these exact strings. Regenerate with
     osascript -l JavaScript extract_audio_strings.js psf
     python3 generate_audio.py --lang psf
   Scene art is shared with the Nepali pack (language-independent scene
   emblems — scenes and symbols only, no depictions of God or of Jesus'
   face). */
